From c815543bc2504eccaae9f6adce5046f41710f38c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:59:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): count external memory prefetch outcomes and
 wait

MemoryManager._prefetch_provider blocks the turn on the external memory
provider for up to the prefetch timeout (8 s), but none of its exits
recorded anything. A provider that times out on most turns only shows up
as a log warning; #124151 had to measure Hindsight's recall by hand to
find that the 8 s bound was dropping prefetch on nearly every turn.

Add hermes.memory.prefetch.count next to hermes.memory.op.count: one row
per external-provider prefetch with
- provider: a bundled memory plugin, else "plugin" (memory.op.count's rule)
- outcome: success / empty / failed / timed_out / skipped (the previous
  call is still running, so this turn did not ask the provider)
- latency_bucket: how long the turn waited on it, in the tool-call buckets

The row is recorded on the caller's thread at each exit, so a stuck call
that returns late adds nothing. The builtin path is unchanged. Opt-in like
the rest of shared metrics; never the query or the recalled text. Schema
and the "what is collected" doc gain the matching entry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
